{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1qBQDS7PGqgKSqGG1RG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I stopped before signing off. The device connection failed partway through, and I have not finished the sweep, so I am not calling this a pass.\n\n**Device status:** every device call (observe, screenshot, wait, open_app) has returned `BrokenPipeError` since I tapped \"Add medicine\" on the \"Miss test\" group form. I could not recover the connection after several retries. The app may still be on that unsaved group form.\n\n**Bugs filed (all three came back \"could not reproduce\"):**\n1. **Calibration: Progesterone result is dropped on save.** I added a Progesterone value (1.2, then 3) with Estradiol and Testosterone. The saved card showed only Estradiol and \"+1 record\" (Testosterone), and Edit test result did not list Progesterone. Reproduced three times. Progesterone may be intentionally unsupported, but then the form should not accept it.\n2. **Home: calibrated Estradiol shows 21 pg/mL.** The same-day lab results were 120–150 pg/mL, and Home shows \"Estradiol · calibrated\" with 21 pg/mL. This may be a model expectation, so it's worth a look rather than a certain bug.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- Medicine category labels: Estradiol, Antiandrogen, SERM, GnRHa and Custom all show the right options and labels.\n- Custom medicine: the empty-name message appears, and a saved medicine shows \"Tablet · 2 mg\" in both the list and details.\n- Group history backdated to Nov 10 with \"Mark as completed\": Nov 10–13 each show one record in Plan, History and the record editor, with the right date and 12:00 AM time. Nov 9 is empty.\n- Once records exist, the group start date is locked and the editor says so.\n- Calibration unit chips match the test subtitles for Estradiol, Testosterone, Progesterone, Prolactin, FSH and LH.\n- Cancelling the add-result form discards it. Rotating the screen on Calibration keeps the data.\n\n**Not tested:** \"Mark as missed\" history generation (the default option), weekly schedules, night-owl mode, archiving, Estradiol unit switching, stock tracking, and app-restart persistence.\n\n**Side effects to clean up:** I created the medicine \"Test Med\" (Custom, 2 mg), the medicine \"Estradiol valerate\" (1 mg), the group \"Oral E2\" (start Nov 10, 3 calibration results on Nov 13, and generated Nov 10–13 records). I may also have left the unsaved \"Miss test\" group form open. I also tapped \"Enable stock tracking\" by mistake and Quick log on Home once. Neither showed any visible change.\n\nIf the device comes back, the next steps are the \"Mark as missed\" check and the untested items above. Until then, I can't sign off."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 350, "cache_read_input_tokens": 252623, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 350}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "7807bf19-6b7f-4cef-94fd-5c29e821fc67", "uuid": "4df9a203-9bfa-4411-92e3-20df8feb4608", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T23:56:17.585Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1qBPwpPAh3Wf7vy4Akh"}
